    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_P07_1088_metodo_2",
      "@type": "art:Metodo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_P07_1088_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 4,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Second, we employ an instance of the distributional hypothesis (Harris, 1985), which can be phrased as follows: different instances of the same semantic relation tend to appear in similar textual contexts."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_tarefa_Grafos_de_conhecimento_ontologias",
      "@type": "art:Mencao",
      "art:frequencia": 3,
      "art:refereSe": {
        "@id": "art:tarefa_Grafos_de_conhecimento_ontologias"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_dyer12_objetivo_2",
      "@type": "art:Objetivo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_dyer12_secao_1"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 5,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We present experiments on learning on 1.5 million training sentences, and show significant improvements over tuning discriminative models on small development sets."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_N18_3011_ref_27",
      "@type": "art:Referencia",
      "art:anoReferencia": {
        "@type": "xsd:gYear",
        "@value": "2017"
      },
      "art:ordem": 27,
      "art:texto": "Chenyan Xiong, Russell Power, and Jamie Callan. 2017. Explicit semantic ranking for academic search via knowledge graph embedding. In WWW."
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_trabalho_futuro_1",
      "@type": "art:TrabalhoFuturo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_secao_7"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 13,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In future work, we plan to explore utilizing our constraints to improve the performance of learned CRF models."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_tarefa_Sumarizacao",
      "@type": "art:Mencao",
      "art:frequencia": 43,
      "art:refereSe": {
        "@id": "art:tarefa_Sumarizacao"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_contribuicao_1",
      "@type": "art:Contribuicao",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 5,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Overall, our contributions are: (1) a 162-paper survey of current human evaluation practices in long-form summarization; (2) LONG EVAL, a set of three guidelines for evaluating faithfulness in long-form summarization; (3) an empirical validation of LONG EVAL guidelines on two long-form summarization datasets in different domains (SQuALITY and PubMed); (4) A dataset with 3-way fine-grained human faithfulness judgments for 120 SQuALITY & PubMed summaries annotated using LONG EVAL which can be used for benchmarking automatic metrics."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_contribuicao_2",
      "@type": "art:Contribuicao",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_secao_7"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 6,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We articulated general, easy-to-enforce constraints on binary, verb-based relation phrases in English that ameliorate these problems and yield richer and more informative relations (see, for example, Table 2)."
      }
    },
