      "art:titulo": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Sparse Information Extraction: Unsupervised Language Models to the Rescue"
      },
      "rdfs:label": "Sparse Information Extraction: Unsupervised Language Models to the Rescue"
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_metodo_2",
      "@type": "art:Metodo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 5,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "To better understand the challenges of human evaluation on long-form summaries (150 words or longer), we first conduct a comprehensive survey of 162 publications and preprints on long-form summarization (Section 2)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_ref_60",
      "@type": "art:Referencia",
      "art:anoReferencia": {
        "@type": "xsd:gYear",
        "@value": "2022"
      },
      "art:ordem": 60,
      "art:texto": "Jason Wei, Maarten Bosma, Vincent Zhao, Kelvin Guu, Adams Wei Yu, Brian Lester, Nan Du, Andrew M Dai, and Quoc V Le. 2022. Finetuned language models are zero-shot learners. In International Conference on Learning Representations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:termo_retell",
      "@type": "art:Termo",
      "art:lema": "retell",
      "art:radical": "retel"
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2020_acl_main_207_termo_6",
      "@type": "art:OcorrenciaTermo",
      "art:doTermo": {
        "@id": "art:termo_embeddings"
      },
      "art:frequencia": 39,
      "art:posicaoRanking": 6
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:temAutor",
      "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty",
      "rdfs:domain": {
        "@id": "art:ArtigoCientifico"
      },
      "rdfs:range": {
        "@id": "art:Autor"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_bohnet09_metodo_1",
      "@type": "art:Metodo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_bohnet09_secao_1"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 4,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Our system combines and implements efficient parsing techniques to get a high accuracy as well as very good parsing and training time."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_objetivo_1",
      "@type": "art:Objetivo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_2023_eacl_main_121_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 3,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "To move towards a more consistent and efficient human evaluation, we present LONG EVAL, a set of guidelines for human evaluation of faithfulness in long-form summarization (Section 3)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_objetivo_1",
      "@type": "art:Objetivo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_secao_1"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 4,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This paper shows that the output of state-ofthe-art Open IE systems is rife with uninformative and incoherent extractions."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_P07_1088_ref_6",
      "@type": "art:Referencia",
      "art:anoReferencia": {
        "@type": "xsd:gYear",
        "@value": "2005"
      },
      "art:ordem": 6,
      "art:texto": "O. Etzioni, M. Cafarella, D. Downey, S. Kok, A. Popescu, T. Shaked, S. Soderland, D. Weld, and A. Y ates. 2005. Unsupervised named-entity extraction from the web: An experimental study. Artificial Intelligence , 165(1):91-134."
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:termo_translation",
      "@type": "art:Termo",
      "art:lema": "translation",
      "art:radical": "translat"
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_dyer12_problema_1",
      "@type": "art:Problema",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_dyer12_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 4,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Features may be lexicalized and sparse, non-local and overlapping, or be designed to generalize beyond surface statistics by incorporating part-of-speech or syntactic labels."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_mooney05_objetivo_1",
      "@type": "art:Objetivo",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_mooney05_secao_1"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 5,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "We introduce a learning semantic parser, SCISSOR , that maps natural-language sentences to a detailed, formal, meaningrepresentation language."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_mooney05_secao_3",
      "@type": "art:OutraSecao",
      "art:numeroPalavras": 232,
      "art:ordem": 3,
      "art:tituloSecao": "2 Target MRL's"
    },
    {
      "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_problema_2",
      "@type": "art:Problema",
      "art:extraidoDe": {
        "@id": "art:artigo_fader11_secao_2"
      },
      "art:pontuacao": 7,
      "art:texto": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Although the syntactic constraint significantly reduces incoherent and uninformative extractions, it allows overly-specific relation phrases such as is offering only modest greenhouse gas reduction targets at."
      }
    },
